drafts/reviews/01-codex.err:697:<p>Now the taxonomy, tested against what this book actually found. The straight line caught him, and caught him where he was most concrete. Essay 2 records the scenario in which the car is replaced by an air-cushion vehicle: the impressive machine of his moment, extended forward. Air-cushion vehicles retreated to a single scheduled route, <!-- CHECK: hovercraft-2000 --> while what displaced the combustion engine kept the wheels, the roads and the shape. <!-- CHECK: ev-share-2025 --> Essay 3 records the same shape in a different register — that contact would need investment beyond nuclear-energy research, an extrapolation from the cost curve of big physics that was wrong by two orders of magnitude. <!-- CHECK: breakthrough-listen-2015 --></p>
drafts/reviews/01-codex.err:698:<p>The sudden turn caught him harder, and it is the mode this book keeps recording. He did not see that competence would be grown from written language at scale; essay 4 files that as the omission the whole book turns on, and essay 7 finds him betting explicitly against the formalism that produced it. <!-- CHECK: gpt3-2020 --> He did not see that the unit of selection in human heredity would move from the couple to the embryo, which is essay 8's central finding: his machine screens partners, and what arrived screens embryos. <!-- CHECK: embryo-screening-2024 --> Both are Athena from the head of Zeus. Neither was available to be extrapolated from anything on his desk.</p>
