1647-loops mediated by neurotransmitters, systems that have no physical
1648-analogues in computers. Damasio makes the point that these messages also provide content for the mind, especially emotions and
1649-feelings: “relative to the brain, the body provides more than mere
1650-support and modulation: it provides a basic topic for brain representations” (xvii). It is precisely the disruption of this normal integration between mind and body that makes the intuition of Lem’s
