chapters/03-who-pays-for-the-telescope.html-6-<title>3 · Who pays for the telescope — Sixty Years Later</title>
chapters/03-who-pays-for-the-telescope.html:7:<meta name="description" content="Lem asks why the sky is silent, answers it in an endnote, and then spends two pages on the part nobody quotes: what the search costs, who would pay, who would transmit, and why an efficiently coded message is indistinguishable from noise. Sixty years on, the search has covered a drinking glass of the ocean.">
